      "reasons": [
        "The packet supports that gender schema relates to internalization of gender stereotypes and sensitivity to gender stereotypical attributes, but it does not explicitly define gender schema as “a person’s internalized set of gender stereotypes” or spell out that it “shapes how sensitive they are to traits and information seen as typical of males or females.”",
        "While the packet reports that stereotypically incongruent sentences were rated as less meaningful and less probable to use (supporting the idea that stereotype violations affect language perception/naturalness), it does not provide the full phrasing about “making stereotype-inconsistent statements seem less natural or likely” as a defining mechanism of gender schema."
